Step 1: Download FFmpeg
Go to: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html
Click Windows
Download from “Windows builds” (usually takes you to gyan.dev)
Download the ZIP file (full build)

Step 2: Extract it
Right-click the ZIP file → Extract All
Open the extracted folder
You’ll see a folder like:
ffmpeg-xxxx
Go inside → open bin folder
You should see:
ffmpeg.exe
This is the main file

Step 3: Put your videos in one place
Create a new folder (example: merge_videos)
Copy all your 450 .mp4 files into it
👉 Make sure:
Files are named in order (very important!)
Example:
video1.mp4
video2.mp4
video3.mp4
...

Step 4: Create the list file

Inside that same folder:

Right click → New → Text Document
Name it:
list.txt
Open it and paste like this:
file 'video1.mp4'
file 'video2.mp4'
file 'video3.mp4'
...

Step 5: Open Command Prompt in that folder
Open your folder
Click on the address bar
Type:
cmd
Press Enter

Step 6: Run the merge command

Now paste this:

"path_to_ffmpeg\ffmpeg.exe" -f concat -safe 0 -i list.txt -c copy output.mp4 

Step 7: Wait
It will process quickly (few minutes max)
You’ll get:
output.mp4

🎉 Done — your full video is ready  

